HANDOVER.md

# Models and their textures ARE tracked, deliberately.
#
# They used to be kept out because they are large, with two hand-written
# placeholders left in so a clone had something to draw. That stopped being a
# sensible trade once the game started depending on them: a fresh clone built
# and ran, but the aircraft, the camps and the gun vehicles were all missing, so
# what it produced was not the game. An asset the game needs to be itself
# belongs with the code that needs it.
#
# The whole folder is about 11 MB, which is nothing next to the dependencies
# CMake downloads on the first configure.
#
# Worth knowing: git keeps every version of a binary for ever, and cannot pack
# them the way it packs text. Swapping a 6 MB model repeatedly grows the
# repository by 6 MB each time, and deleting the file later does not shrink it
# again. Settling on a model before committing it costs nothing; churning
# through several does.